.TH TODO 1 "2026-10-13" "Todo CLI 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
todo \- manage Microsoft To Do items from the command line or a full-screen terminal UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B todo
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B todo tui
.br
.B todo
.RB { \-h | \-H | \-\-help | \-\-HELP | \-? }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B todo
reads and changes your Microsoft To Do lists. Run with a subcommand it works as a conventional command-line
tool. Run with no arguments in an interactive terminal, or with
.BR "todo tui" ,
it opens a full-screen, keyboard-driven terminal UI that follows the Common User Access (CUA) conventions.
.PP
The first use opens a browser window to sign in to your Microsoft account. Access tokens are refreshed
automatically.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "add item " subject
Add an item. Options:
.BI \-\-list " name"
(target list),
.B \-\-star
(mark important),
.BI \-\-due\-date " date"
(\fByyyy\-MM\-dd\fR or \fBMM\-dd\fR).
.TP
.BI "add list " name
Add a list.
.TP
.B list
List items. Options:
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
(include completed),
.B \-\-no\-status
and
.BR \-\-older\-than .
.TP
.BI complete " id"
Mark an item as completed.
.TP
.B remove
Remove items.
.TP
.B tui
Open the terminal UI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIInteractive\fR|\fIJson\fR
Output format for the command-line commands.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-HELP ", " \-?
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH TERMINAL UI
The UI has a title bar, a menu bar, a context line (list, counts, filter, and how many items are scrolled out
of view), the item list, a status line, and a key bar of the commands available. It adapts to the terminal
size and shows a warning below 60 columns by 12 rows.
.SS Keys
Custom commands use Alt plus a letter. Where Alt cannot be confirmed, the Ctrl alternative is shown instead.
Both always work.
.TP
.BR Alt+N " / " Ctrl+N
New item.
.TP
.BR Alt+M " / " Ctrl+E ", " Enter
Modify the selected item.
.TP
.BR Space ", " Alt+C " / " Ctrl+T
Complete or reopen the selected item.
.TP
.BR Alt+I " / " Ctrl+P
Mark or unmark the item as important.
.TP
.BR Delete ", " Alt+R " / " Ctrl+R
Remove the item after confirmation.
.TP
.BR Alt+L " / " Ctrl+L
Choose which list is shown.
.TP
.BR ? ", " Alt+S " / " Ctrl+F
Search by subject.
.TP
.BR Alt+A " / " Ctrl+A
Show or hide completed items.
.TP
.BR Alt+O " / " Ctrl+O
Choose a color theme. The colors preview as the selection moves; Enter applies and saves, Esc restores.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the selected subject. In text fields it copies the selection.
.TP
.B F1
Help.
.TP
.BR F3 ", " Alt+X
Exit. In a dialog, F3 closes the dialog.
.TP
.B F5
Reload from Microsoft To Do.
.TP
.BR F7 ", " F8 ", " PgUp ", " PgDn
Page up or down.
.TP
.B F10
Move to the menu bar. Alt+T, Alt+F, Alt+E, Alt+V and Alt+H open menus.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Move between controls.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel a dialog or close a menu. It does not exit the program.
.PP
Ctrl+Q is not used because terminals reserve it for flow control.
.SS Item form
Subject is required. Due date is optional (\fByyyy\-MM\-dd\fR or \fBMM\-dd\fR); an empty value clears it.
The list can only be chosen when adding. OK stays disabled until the form is valid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I appsettings.json
Optional, next to the executable. The
.B Tui
section sets
.B AltKeys
(\fBauto\fR, \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR),
.B Theme
(\fBDefault\fR, \fBOne Dark Pro\fR, \fBDracula\fR, \fBTokyo Night\fR, \fBCatppuccin Mocha\fR,
\fBGitHub Dark\fR, \fBNight Owl\fR, \fBGruvbox Material\fR, \fBSynthWave '84\fR) and optional
.B Palette
overrides of single colors (names or hex).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/todo/settings.json
Per-user settings written when a theme is chosen in the UI (\fI~/.config/todo/settings.json\fR on Linux,
\fI%APPDATA%\\todo\\settings.json\fR on Windows). It overrides appsettings.json.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI TODO_ name
Overrides a setting from
.IR appsettings.json ,
using
.B __
as the section separator, for example
.BR TODO_Tui__AltKeys=on .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any non-empty value selects a monochrome display.
.TP
.BR LANG ", " LC_ALL
Without a UTF-8 locale the UI uses ASCII symbols.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command or the UI failed.
.TP
.B 2
.B todo tui
was started without an interactive terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md and docs/help.html in the source repository.
